prompt_stages.gemini_fact_extraction:
You are a scientific data extraction engine. Analyze the provided RSS science news payload. Extract the core scientific discovery or phenomenon, every concrete quantitative fact/metric actually present (an empty numbers array is valid when none occurs), any key research entities/institutes mentioned, and the primary tone of the article. Return a JSON object matching this exact schema: {{"facts": [{{"fact_id": "F01", "claim": "fact 1", "source_spans": [{{"field": "full_text", "start": 0, "end": 6, "quote": "fact 1"}}]}}], "numbers": [], "tone": "optimistic/foreboding/etc", "entities": []}}. Do not include markdown wraps or explanations.

Payload:
{payload_text}

prompt_stages.gemini_scene_rewrite:
You are a script doctor. Rewrite the dialogue lines to resolve these critiques: {feedback}. If the critique says a fact is stated inaccurately, you MUST restate that fact in the SOURCE'S OWN WORDING from the fact index -- delete the inaccurate phrasing from the previous draft entirely. Do not keep it, do not soften it, and do not swap in a more evocative synonym: a phrase that sounds better but changes the claim is the defect. Retaining the outline's structure does NOT mean retaining wording the critique rejected. Incorporate the original science facts: {facts}. Retain the exact outline structure: {scene_outline}. Below is the previous failed draft lines for reference:
{previous_draft}
Return JSON with EXACTLY the same keys as the draft schema and no others: {{"lines": [{{"beat_id": "b001", "text": "revised verbatim spoken line...", "fact_uses": [{{"fact_id": "F01", "spoken_claim": "the words in this line that state F01"}}], "non_fact": false}}]}}. Do not emit a fact_ids field; it is not part of this schema. Keep one line for every beat in the scene -- do not drop or merge a beat while rewriting.
